 "findings": [
  "the gates never receive the key triple: the embedded record the shapers hand over carries record +0x8..+0x30 at its +0x0..+0x28, the chain tag byte at +0x70 and dispatch byte 0 at +0x71; its +0x78..+0x98 slots are written by neither shaper (no access at phase +0x298..+0x2b0 in either body)",
  "on the dispatch-0 arm the shaper-driven gate invocation takes, the gate manufactures the key pair itself: it stores the .rodata pointer \"hl-node\" (0x60f0b2 in gate_c, 0x605ccd in gate_a) at embedded +0x88 and 7 at +0x90, moves the pair to +0x78/+0x80, and calls the key-lookup callee with (tag, \"hl-node\", 7) after its config-slot check; the second gate arm instead moves a pre-existing +0x88/+0x90 pair down to +0x78/+0x80",
  "the lookup callee consumes (tag, pointer, length) without ever using the pointer or length as a memory base: tag 0 returns at once, tags 1/2/3 select the reference string field at global +0xd0/+0xb8/+0xa0, the field is copied out (alloc + memcpy) and handed with the caller key to helper 0x14c2b50; the helper either reports the crit-msg state applied (al = 1, descriptor strings freed) or delegates to equality callee 0x154c4e0; a nonzero verdict only makes the lookup callee emit the \"crit msg initialization not applied\" log record (base/src/crit_msg.rs line 471); no caller tests the result, which does not exist",
  "the chain tag is tested downstream only as the lookup callee's jump-table index and as the gate's post-call zero test (gate_c: test r15b,r15b at 0x2cb690d, immediately before the +0x11c outcome-byte compares at 0x2cb6912; gate_a mirrors both); the key bytes are compared nowhere in any traced body - the only byte equality is delegated one level below the lookup callee, to 0x154c4e0",
  "after placement, the shapers read the triple again only to free it: guarded exit arms dealloc the lookup_d allocation through the spread pair (len at phase +0xa8, pointer at +0xb0) and through the record pair (len at +0x88, pointer at +0x90); the tag qword at phase +0xa0 is loaded once per shaper to form the lookup call's tag argument"
 ],
